2026-05-04T06:16:21.320Z JOY-015A-FD comment.added "Phase 2 (implementation) complete. Sub-phases:\n\n(2a) Filter/sidecar rollback. crypt_filter.rs deleted, Filter subcommand removed, setup_git_filter and ensure_gitattributes_for_item removed, save_zone_keys / load_zone_keys / cache_zone_keys removed. Session file no longer holds Crypt secrets. CryptCommand::List + ZoneCommand::List renamed to Ls per Joy convention.\n\n(2b) ZoneAccessDenied + transparent decrypt. New JoyError::ZoneAccessDenied { zone } variant. joy_core::crypt has a thread-local active-zone-keys context (set_active_zone_keys / clear_active_zone_keys / active_zone_key / has_active_zone_keys). store::read_yaml peeks for the JOYCRYPT magic and decrypts via the active context before serde_yaml; missing zone surfaces as ZoneAccessDenied.\n\n(2c) Encrypt-on-disk in joy crypt add/rm. items::save_item now uses an internal write_item_file that encrypts when item.crypt_zone is set, atomic via temp + rename. run_add / run_rm / run_add_all / run_rm_all walk through update_item with the active zone key installed. Free-file paths walk crypt.zones[].paths with resolve_target_paths (file or recursive directory), encrypt_file_in_place / decrypt_file_in_place per file. Persist-wrap-first ordering for crash safety.\n\n(2d) Free-file verbs. joy crypt read (decrypt to stdout), write (encrypt stdin), edit ($EDITOR on temp), unlock (decrypt in place), lock (re-encrypt). All run via a fresh per-command unlock_for_file path - passphrase prompt every time, seed in memory only for the command's lifetime, no persisted secrets.\n\n(2e) Auto re-lock walk in joy auth. After a successful passphrase verification, walk crypt.zones[].paths for every zone the member has a wrap for, encrypt any file currently in plaintext, print 'Re-locked N file(s).' Best-effort, no daemon - the next joy auth (or any other crypto-touching joy command via crypt_session::ensure_zone_keys) does the same opportunistic walk.\n\n(crypt_session helper) New joy-cli/src/crypt_session.rs with ensure_zone_keys() that any read command (joy show, joy ls) calls upfront. No-op on plain projects; populates the thread-local context for projects with Crypt activity. joy show and joy ls grew an optional --passphrase flag that hooks into this.\n\nTests: 310 joy-core, 88 joy-cli unit tests; 304 bats integration tests including the new crypt e2e (read/write/edit/lock/unlock roundtrips, joy show on encrypted item, joy auth re-lock). cargo fmt + cargo clippy --all-D warnings both green. Phase 3 (Tutorial + website docs) follows next." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
